{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/optouttracking()"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optOutTracking()"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Opts the user out of all tracking, and returns once the SDK has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applied it: from then on ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)"},{"text":". Does nothing if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user is already opted out. The choice persists across launches.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"optOutTracking","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Queued events and People updates are deleted, not sent, and the local","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity is reset. This does not wait for the network.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An upload already in progress is not cancelled. The SDK checks consent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when a flush starts and before it moves from events to People updates,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but not between requests. A flush that is already sending events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"therefore still sends every event it had read: for a full flush such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/flush()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", that is the whole event queue, 50 per request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This does not delete the user’s Mixpanel profile or data."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"The SDK’s own opt-out queues a profile deletion but never sends it —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the leftover request would later delete the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"next","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" identified user’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"profile instead — so the adapter discards it with the rest of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queue. To erase a user’s data, use Mixpanel’s GDPR deletion API from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your server.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"optOutTracking()","externalID":"s:23SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics0bC7ServiceV14optOutTrackingyyYaF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"optOutTracking","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"symbolKind":"method"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"optInTracking"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"distinctID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"properties"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SwiduxAnalytics0B5ValueO","text":"AnalyticsValue","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"title":"optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/optintracking(distinctid:properties:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","abstract":[{"text":"Opts the user back into tracking and returns once the SDK has applied","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" issued straight afterwards is honored.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/optOutTracking()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"optOutTracking"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"title":"optOutTracking()","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/optouttracking()","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optOutTracking()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Opts the user out of all tracking, and returns once the SDK has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied it: from then on "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are dropped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Does nothing if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"user is already opted out. The choice persists across launches."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"text":" internally so apps never need to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"}],"title":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","abstract":[{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that owns and forwards to a Mixpanel SDK"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/flush()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"flush"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"title":"flush()","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/flush()","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/flush()","abstract":[{"text":"Sends every queued event and People update via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelInstance.flush(performFullFlush:completion:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and returns once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the SDK reports completion — not just the first 50-record batch the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SDK’s default flush sends.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"}}}